reference.api:
```
POST /v1/conversations                         → {conversation_id}
POST /v1/conversations/{id}/messages           {parent_id, content, client_msg_id, model}
     → 200 text/event-stream: delta events …, then done {message_id, usage}
GET  /v1/conversations/{id}/messages/{mid}/stream?from=n   (resume a stream)
POST /v1/messages/{mid}/stop
GET  /v1/conversations?cursor=                 → list for sidebar
```
- `client_msg_id` makes a retried send idempotent. Responses stream as **Server-Sent Events**: traffic is one-way, it works through proxies and reconnects with `Last-Event-ID`. WebSockets add little here, since sends are ordinary POSTs.
